      "attempt": 1,
      "root_cause": "The document access function lacks an ownership ownership check, allowing unauthorized access.",
      "explanation": "An ownership-m mismatch if statement comparing the existing document owner ID with requesting_user_id should be added added to ensure that only the owner of a document can access it. If there the ownership does not match, a PermissionError should be raised.",
      "patch_format": "unified_diff",
      "patch_text": "diff --git a/app/access.py b/app/access.py\n--- a/app/access.py\n+++ b/app/access.py\n@@ -33,4 +33,6 @@\n \n     # VULNERABLE IMPLEMENTATION (Broken Object-Level Authorization):\n     # Fails to enforce that doc[\"owner_id\"] == requesting_user_id before returning.\n+    if doc['owner_id'] != requesting_user_id:\n+        raise PermissionError('Ownership mismatch: user is not authorized to access this document document')\n     return dict(doc)\n",
      "patch_hash": "sha256:e0982cc538ca82a517c51898313be0be9b50c19aa934afbaad4483b9260f6956",
